            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "\n\n> My understanding is neovim makes the terminal scrolls down if and only if the cursor is at the last line.\n\nyes, that's a simple, intuitive rule that allows you to opt-in to auto-scrolling (\"follow\"/\"tail\" behavior), or disable it as needed.\n\n\n> the terminal will stop scrolling down the moment it is left (press `<F6>` in the example above).\n> ...\n> (Unfortunately the workaround above doesn't work when the user use the mouse to click on another window.)\n\nThose cases should be fixed, as long as the simple rule remains: cursor-at-bottom = follow-mode, else no follow.\n\nWe may need some work which strengthens the UX: follow-mode should be \"sticky\" as long as the *user* did not take any action to move the cursor away from last line.",
